6. AGRICULTURAL PRODUCT CATALOG
==================================================

Product search is a major feature.

When a farmer searches for wheat seeds, show:
- Actual product or notified variety name.
- Genuine product image from a permitted catalog or seller source.
- Manufacturer or brand.
- Product category and package size.
- Verified agronomic characteristics.
- Suitable region and season when documented.
- Official source or seller link.
- Price and stock only when actually available.
- Data source and last-checked timestamp.

Do not generate fictional product names or images and label them as real products.

Separate agricultural varieties from commercial packaged products. A notified variety may exist without a current seller listing.

Build a provider adapter architecture so catalog sources can be added without rewriting the application.

If no live product API is available, display verified catalog records and outbound source links. Clearly state that current stock and price have not been verified.

"Best seed" recommendations must account for region, season, soil, irrigation, and crop objectives. Do not make universal superiority claims.

