9. CROP AND IRRIGATION RECOMMENDATION ENGINE
==================================================

Build a transparent recommendation engine using:
- Crop and growth stage.
- Sowing date.
- Farm location.
- Soil type and available soil-test data.
- Irrigation method.
- Soil moisture if available.
- Recent and forecast rainfall.
- Temperature and relevant weather conditions.
- Last irrigation event.
- Verified agronomic guidance.

Each recommendation must contain:
- Recommendation text.
- Preferred language.
- Supporting inputs.
- Explanation of why the recommendation was made.
- Missing inputs and assumptions.
- Source references.
- Generated timestamp.
- Confidence or uncertainty where it can be meaningfully justified.
- Appropriate safety or expert-verification notes.

Do not use an LLM alone to invent irrigation schedules or fertilizer quantities.

Use deterministic, testable rules based on vetted agricultural guidance for supported cases. If critical information is missing, ask follow-up questions or provide cautious general guidance.

For crop recommendations, show multiple ranked options, the reason for each ranking, and the conditions under which it may be suitable.

